1
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:44,377
And there's a possiblity that what
we're looking for is in here.

2
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,845
- Yes, sir.
- Let's move!

3
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,894
<i>What's really happening to him?</i>

4
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:04,731
I spend my whole life
looking for that bomb.

5
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:10,028
Do you think Angelito got exposed
to that bomb's radiation?

6
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,143
Should I tell them?

7
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:46,314
Run!

8
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:50,735
Get inside the house!

9
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,238
Everything in their house!

10
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:12,841
Where are you going?

11
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,017
Everything will be okay.

12
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:25,645
We'll save your brother.

13
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:39,826
Sofie…

14
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:41,661
What happened?

15
00:02:41,744 --> 00:02:42,871
- Come on.
- Huh?

16
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,123
What is going on?

17
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:16,696
Viktor Valtrovi.

18
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:04,744
Agent Sianong, the bomb squad
is on the way.

19
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:11,751
All right. Stay safe.

20
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:21,344
- Where is it?!
- Stop!

21
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,599
It's here!

22
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:28,518
We found what we're looking for!

23
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,744
Those are La Morte's men.

24
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,123
What should we do?

25
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:35,501
Bro, what's that?

26
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:36,544
Let's back off.

27
00:05:37,128 --> 00:05:38,921
No, keep going.

28
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:41,215
Are you okay, sweetheart?

29
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:43,843
I'm okay.

30
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,112
You know, if you keep pacing like that,
you'll wear a hole in the floor.

31
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:51,994
I'm getting dizzy for the poor floor.

32
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:54,372
Viktor.

33
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,667
I'm just worried.

34
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:59,293
I'm so worried, my love.

35
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:02,130
Me too.

36
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:55,850
Hey.

37
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,858
It won't start. Hey, it's smoking.

38
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,109
Let's check it.

39
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:15,995
I think the radiator got hit.

40
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,849
Help me.

41
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:38,726
Let's cover it.

42
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,895
Easy.

43
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:01,225
We can't.

44
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,102
Why not?!

45
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,408
Chiara, we have protocols, right?

46
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:20,369
That's what the bomb squad is for.
They're trained to handle this.

47
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:24,290
They're not even here yet.

48
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:28,085
Then we'll do it ourselves. Let's go!

49
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,570
The tip was legit.

50
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:04,705
It's not our job or our mission

51
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:07,166
to retrieve that weapon
of mass destruction. Okay?

52
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:11,087
Our mission is to make sure
Angelito and Sofie are safe.

53
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:18,427
If they get that bomb, we're all dead!

54
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:22,223
If we can't even make sure
those two are safe,

55
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:23,974
we're also risking their lives.

56
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:51,043
Let's go, Angelito. Hurry.

57
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,461
Stay here.

58
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,673
Are you okay?

59
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:58,050
I'm okay.

60
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,431
This can't happen.

61
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,184
What can't?

62
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,104
The bomb.

63
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:11,147
The bomb?

64
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:14,442
We can't let them get it.

65
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:18,696
I have a strong feeling
it shouldn't end up in their hands.

66
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:21,866
Sofie, come on.

67
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,910
You're not even sure that's what

68
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,037
your dad's agency is looking for.

69
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:30,749
Angelito, we have to do something.

70
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,129
We'll stay here.

71
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,261
We can't do that, Angelito.

72
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:44,722
We can't always play it safe.

73
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:46,640
Sometimes we have to take risks.

74
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:51,729
Do you know, Sofie,
how dangerous this is? Look!

75
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:54,064
They have so many guns.

76
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:55,900
It's way too dangerous!

77
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:59,653
Agent Dara, still nothing?

78
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,447
I've tried three radio channels.

79
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:03,741
Maybe they're just in a dead zone.

80
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:07,620
Sofie told me
the signal is weak over there.

81
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,413
I hope that's all it is.

82
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:11,916
Try a different frequency.

83
00:13:17,254 --> 00:13:19,215
Team, please respond.

84
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:25,387
Mikoy!

85
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:26,680
Sianong!

86
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,974
This might be our only chance.

87
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:30,559
Don't you get it?

88
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:33,229
You're both right.

89
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,064
That's the problem.

90
00:13:35,689 --> 00:13:38,192
If we were here for someone else,
this would've been easier.

91
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,194
But we're not.

92
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:42,988
Angelito is my brother.

93
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:46,825
And Sofie is General Ruiz's daughter.

94
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,371
We have to find them.

95
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:54,583
But we can't let that leave either.

96
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,255
Looks like they're leaving. Yes.

97
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:00,839
- They're leaving?
- Yes.

98
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,342
Thank goodness.

99
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:05,261
What do you mean?

100
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,179
Thank goodness.

101
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:09,265
We're finally getting out of here.

102
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:13,269
We still have to find
Laurence and Luisa Mae.

103
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:15,187
Who knows what happened to them.

104
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:22,820
Something?

105
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:23,946
Sofie.

106
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:26,740
If we do anything else,

107
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:29,159
we might never make it out of here.

108
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:31,537
Who knows what could happen to us.

109
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:37,001
You know what, Angelito?
You're such a coward!

110
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:39,670
Sofie!

111
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:41,922
You can't do that!

112
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:50,306
Come on, hurry!

113
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,473
Hurry!

114
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,642
Angelito!

115
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:57,938
What's that?

116
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:00,983
Angelito!

117
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:03,944
Stop!

118
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:06,614
- Mikoy!
- Mikoy, wait!

119
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:11,869
Chiara!

120
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:12,786
Let's go!

121
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,622
Go. I'll handle the bomb!

122
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,792
It's um…

123
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,126
a wild boar.

124
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,474
Hurry up!

125
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:19,770
Hurry.

126
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:28,445
What?

127
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,363
Have you found them?

128
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:31,115
- They're not here.
- Not here either.

129
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:32,700
Let's check over here.

130
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,288
What a shame.

131
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:55,824
Angelito. Hurry up.

132
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:57,659
Let's stay here for now.

133
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,788
Come on, Angelito.

134
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,081
Hurry up.

135
00:18:03,415 --> 00:18:04,750
Come here.

136
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:17,221
What?

137
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:18,430
Did you see them?

138
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:19,932
- They're not here.
- They disappeared.

139
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,934
Let's split up.

140
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:23,811
You go that way. We'll go this way.

141
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:25,687
Let's go!

142
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:38,700
Brusko.

143
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,092
Keep your voice down.

144
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,640
Keep your voice down.

145
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:44,600
Lady Amor.

146
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,019
Yes. Follow me.

147
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:48,061
Okay.

148
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:49,646
Come on, Angelito.

149
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:50,647
Come on, come on.

150
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,691
Easy now.

151
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,152
Over here.

152
00:19:57,821 --> 00:19:58,655
All right.

153
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:02,743
Where are we going?

154
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:34,274
Your parents will be so happy.

155
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:36,235
So much has happened.

156
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,945
The bomb is here.

157
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:39,488
Ms. Italy took it.

158
00:20:39,571 --> 00:20:41,657
Now you're here too, huh?

159
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,742
Was this your plan all along?

160
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:45,535
You're the one who tipped them off.

161
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,329
Because Viktor never told me anything.

162
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,124
Why do you look so angry?

163
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,629
Why would I be angry?

164
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,383
Yes, why would you be?

165
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,472
Peace! We're on the same side!

166
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,395
- They came this way, right?
- Yes.

167
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:13,272
- Angelito!
- Sofie!

168
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:15,857
- Angelito!
- Where are you?

169
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:16,942
Sofie.

170
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:18,360
They went through here, right?

171
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:19,486
Yes!

172
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:22,572
Sofie!

173
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:23,740
Angelito!

174
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:26,118
Where are you two? Come out!

175
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:29,830
Sofie!

176
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:33,083
Take cover! Take cover! Mikoy!

177
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:18,420
- I'm out of ammo.
- Me too.

178
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:48,909
<i>What are we gonna do, Viktor?</i>

179
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:29,825
Sianong!
